# Declarative problem authored by the small model for
# "Carina is a parent of Ana. Who is Carina a parent of?". The model saw only
# the message: it writes strings, the host links them to the lexicon. One
# statement the message asserts, one assumption the model added (parenthood
# is asymmetric, so Ana is not a parent of Carina: general world knowledge,
# written with the statement's own relation phrase), one question. No solve, cnl, resolve or remember appears here; the host compiles
# those steps into an inspectable execution circuit and, by default, reports
# the assumption without using it.
@context stated
  relation "parent of"
  role subject "Carina"
  role object "Ana"
  polarity affirmed
  certainty asserted

@background assumed
  relation "parent of"
  role subject "Ana"
  role object "Carina"
  polarity negated
  basis world

@question query
  where match
    relation "parent of"
    role subject "Carina"
    role object ?who
    polarity affirmed
  end
  select ?who
